node_modules
.pnpm-store/
node-compile-cache/
*.log*
.nuxt
# Isolated build dir for the check chain (NUXT_BUILD_DIR=.nuxt-check) so it
# never collides with a parked `nuxt dev`. The bare `.nuxt` above matches only
# that exact name.
.nuxt-check
# Same idea for the `lt dev test` stack: the `cli` exports
# NUXT_BUILD_DIR=.nuxt-test for its app process, because the Nuxt lock sits on
# the build dir and a shared one made the test build abort against a parked
# `nuxt dev`. Nothing in this repo writes the dir — the entry is still required.
.nuxt-test
.nitro
.cache
.output
# DEV-2724: the Nitro OUTPUT dir of the `lt dev test` stack — an axis of its own,
# independent of the build dirs above. `lt dev test` serves the production bundle
# and so rebuilds on every run, which used to overwrite the `.output` a local
# `pnpm run build` left behind. Set by the `cli` (NITRO_OUTPUT_DIR), not by a
# script here; the guard in tests/unit/nuxt-builddir-isolation.test.ts is what
# ties this entry to a reason.
.output-test
# Catch-all beneath the named entries above. `NUXT_BUILD_DIR` / `NITRO_OUTPUT_DIR`
# make `.nuxt-<x>` / `.output-<x>` trivial to spawn, so enumerating names is
# structurally incomplete — a manual `.nuxt-perf` / `.output-perf` profiling run was
# the first one nobody had written an entry for, and it put 460 untracked files in
# `git status` and walked `oxfmt` into generated bundles. The named entries stay:
# they carry the reason each dir exists, and the unit guard asserts them one by one.
# (`.nuxtrc` is checked in and has no dash — it is not matched.)
.nuxt-*
.output-*
.env
dist
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
